SAP BTP (Business Technology Platform) is the core cloud platform, while the BTP Cockpit is its
web-based user interface for managing and administering BTP accounts and resources.
Think of BTP as the engine, and the Cockpit as the dashboard you use to control and monitor it.

SAP Business Technology Platform (BTP):
---------------------------------------
-> It's a comprehensive cloud platform that offers a wide range of services and capabilities for building,
   extending, and connecting applications.
-> BTP acts as the foundation for cloud solutions, enabling businesses to extend SAP systems and
   connect various cloud and on-premise systems.
-> BTP is used to build new applications, extend existing ones, integrate systems, and manage data.

SAP BTP Cockpit:
----------------
-> It's the central web-based user interface for administrators and developers to manage and
   administer their SAP BTP accounts.
-> The Cockpit provides access to various functions, including managing applications, services,
    security, and resources.
-> It's the primary tool for creating and managing resources on BTP, including applications,
    services, and security settings.
-> Administrators can use the Cockpit to onboard users, assign roles, and manage access permissions
   within their BTP accounts.
-> The Cockpit also provides a dashboard for monitoring the status of applications and services
   deployed on BTP.

In essence, BTP is the platform, while the Cockpit is the interface you use to interact with
and manage the platform. The Cockpit provides a graphical user interface for managing BTP
resources, while the BTP CLI and APIs offer alternative ways to manage resources at the
command line or programmatically, respectively.